WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:05.631
(intense dramatic music)

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:17.059
 [JFK] But why, some say,
the moon?

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:20.729
Why choose this
as our goal?

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:24.316
 And they may well ask, why
 climb the highest mountain?

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:29.988
Why 35 years ago...

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:31.782
 (alarms beeping)

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.742
(digital glitching)

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:34.952
...fly the Atlantic?

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:39.540
 We choose to go to the moon
and do the other things.

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.752
 Not because they are easy,

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:47.673
(wind whooshing)

00:00:47.673 --> 00:00:50.133
 but because they are hard.

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:52.594
(water rushing)

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:56.723
(ominous music)

00:00:58.642 --> 00:00:59.977
(ground crumbling)

00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:01.979
(distant explosion)

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.941
(eerie music)

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.117
(woman screaming)

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:22.124
(pounding music)

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.214
  [Voice Over Radio]
Houston we're experiencing

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:30.590
some kind of malfunction.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.925
 Houston, do you copy?

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.135
Houston, do you--

